+## Six families, and the three passes that were withdrawn
+
+Six contract families are wired: the read family (108 instances), the allocator (5), copy (2), the
+two exported accessors (2), the four emitted decoders, and `requireCanonicalOffsets`. Five of those
+were wired independently and each reported its own totals; **the totals above are lower than the sum
+of theirs, and deliberately so.**
+
+Three cells that each family reported as a pass rest on a conjunct no run can fail, and are reported
+here as gaps naming it:
+
+* **`rawAlloc` (0), column 2** — Row A binds `bytes`/`alignment` to `x10`/`x11`, the very registers
+  `preAlloc` names, so both register conjuncts are `x == x`
+  (`register_conjunct_is_a_tautology_at_a_reg_binding`).
+* **`memcpy` (139) and `memmove` (140), column 2** — the same thing for `dst`/`src`/`n` against
+  `x10`/`x11`/`x12`, on top of two witness-constructed conjuncts.
+* **`rawAlloc` (0), column 4** — `postAlloc`'s `address ≠ 0`, `alignment ≠ 0` and
+  `address % alignment = 0` mention no captured state at all (`postAllocSuccessB_splits`).
