+## What licenses the two remaining `post` passes
+
+Every mirror in this module was originally stated as `Prop → mirror = true`, which licenses
+**refutation only**: `mirror = false` refutes the predicate, and `mirror = true` says nothing. That
+is not enough to print `ok` in column 4. `memoryBytesB_iff`, `codeIntactB_iff` and
+`noAllocationB_iff` supply the missing direction for the three primitives every `post` shape is
+built from, and `postCopyCheckedB_iff_postCopy`, `postScalarReadCheckedB_iff_postScalarRead` and
+`postBytesAtCheckedB_iff_postBytesAt` lift them to full equivalences. Only the copy rows actually
+reach `ok`, and only those equivalences make that reading legitimate.
 
