+/-! ## The tautology gates
+
+Three verdict paths below would otherwise report an `ok` that rests on a conjunct no run can fail.
+Each is gated here, once, so the gate is visible rather than buried in a dispatch arm. A gate never
+suppresses a **refutation**: the mirrors report the first *failing* conjunct, an unfalsifiable
+conjunct never fails, so any clause a mirror names is one of the real ones. Only the passing
+direction is downgraded. -/
+
+/-- Whether Row A binds `name` at `index` to integer register `number` — i.e. whether the conjunct
+`xnumber = name` is `x == x` here (`register_conjunct_is_a_tautology_at_a_reg_binding`). -/
+def bindingIsTautologicalAt (index : Nat) (name : String) (number : Nat) : Bool :=
+  match bindingRow? index name with
+  | some row => bindingNamesRegister row number
+  | none => false
+
+/-- The `preCopy` register conjuncts that are `x == x` at this instance, by name. -/
+def copyTautologicalRegisterConjuncts (index : Nat) : List String :=
+  (if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "dst" 10 then ["preCopy.x10=destination"] else []) ++
+    (if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "src" 11 then ["preCopy.x11=source"] else []) ++
+    (if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "n" 12 then ["preCopy.x12=length"] else [])
+
+/-- The `preAlloc` register conjuncts that are `x == x` at this instance, by name. Both parameter
+spellings are tried, exactly as `allocBytesBindingRow?` does. -/
+def allocTautologicalRegisterConjuncts (index : Nat) : List String :=
+  (if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "bytes" 10 || bindingIsTautologicalAt index "len" 10 then
+      ["preAlloc.x10=bytes"] else []) ++
+    (if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "alignment" 11 then ["preAlloc.x11=alignment"] else [])
+
+/-- Column 2 for a copy-family instance.
+
+`preCopy` has six conjuncts and `memcpy` a seventh. Two are witness-constructed
+(`MemoryBytes(source)` and `contents.size=length`: `contents` is a ghost byte sequence with no
+binding anywhere, read out of memory at `src`). Three more are `x == x` whenever Row A binds
+`dst`/`src`/`n` to `x10`/`x11`/`x12`, which it does at **both** copy instances. That leaves
+`preCopy.CodeIntact`, and for `memcpy` the non-overlap disjunct, as the only conjuncts a run can
+fail — so "nothing failed" is not a statement that `preCopy` holds and is reported as a gap naming
+exactly what could not fail. A refutation still stands: it can only have come from one of the two
+real conjuncts. -/
+def copyPreVerdict (family : CopyFamily) (index : Nat) (s : State) : Verdict :=
+  match copyArgs? index s with
+  | none => .gap ("Row A dst/src/n bindings are not all evaluable here, or the source slice is"
+      ++ " unmaterialisable; no preCopy conjunct evaluated")
+  | some cargs =>
+    match copyPreFailure? family cargs s with
+    | some clause => .violated clause
+    | none =>
+      match copyTautologicalRegisterConjuncts index with
+      | [] =>
+        -- No register conjunct degenerates here, so the pass is the read family's `@witness-args`
+        -- shape: only `MemoryBytes(source)` and `contents.size=length` are construction-true.
+        .ok
+      | tautologies =>
+        .gap ("preCopy.CodeIntact holds"
+          ++ (match family with | .memcpy => " and memcpy.pre.nonOverlap holds" | .memmove => "")
+          ++ "; MemoryBytes(source) and contents.size=length are witness-constructed; "
+          ++ String.intercalate "/" tautologies
+          ++ " are x == x because Row A binds dst/src/n to the very registers preCopy names, so they"
+          ++ " cannot fail and this is NOT a pass")
+
+/-- Column 2 for an allocator-family instance, with the same gate.
+
+At index 0 Row A binds `bytes` to `x10` and `alignment` to `x11` — the registers `preAlloc` itself
+names — so both register conjuncts are `x == x` and only `CodeIntact` can fail. At index 136 Row A
+binds `len` to `x11` and `alignment` to `x12`, so neither degenerates and the refutation there is
+real. The three `Args = Unit` thunks have `pre = CodeIntact` and nothing to reconstruct, so their
+pass, if the fixture ever reached them, would be a genuine one. -/
+def allocPreVerdictGated (index : Nat) (family : AllocFamily) (s : State) : Verdict :=
+  match family with
+  | .rawAlloc | .allocatorAlloc =>
+    match allocArgs? index s with
+    | none => .gap "Row A binds no evaluable bytes/alignment pair for this instance"
+    | some args =>
+      match preAllocFailure? canonicalEnvironment args s with
+      | some clause => .violated clause
+      | none =>
+        match allocTautologicalRegisterConjuncts index with
+        | [] => .ok
+        | tautologies =>
+          .gap ("preAlloc.CodeIntact holds; " ++ String.intercalate "/" tautologies
+            ++ " are x == x because Row A binds the allocation arguments to the very registers"
+            ++ " preAlloc names, so they cannot fail and this is NOT a pass")
+  | _ =>
+    match preCodeIntactFailure? canonicalEnvironment s with
+    | some clause => .violated clause
+    | none => .ok
+
+/-- Column 4 for an allocator-family instance, with the state-free clauses gated out.
+
+On the success arm three conjuncts — `address ≠ 0`, `alignment ≠ 0` and `address % alignment = 0` —
+are a function of the reconstructed arguments and of the address `contractAlloc.meaning` itself
+returned, and mention no captured state (`postAllocSuccessB_splits`). A pass is therefore reported
+as a gap that names them, and only the machine-dependent clauses are allowed to decide the column.
+On the failure arm `error = outOfMemory` is a tautology for the same reason
+(`alloc_meaning_error_is_always_outOfMemory`), so its pass is gated too; the other three failure-arm
+clauses are real and a refutation from any of them stands. -/
+def allocPostVerdictGated (index : Nat) (family : AllocFamily) (before after : State) : Verdict :=
+  match family with
+  | .rawAlloc | .allocatorAlloc =>
+    match allocArgs? index before with
+    | none => .gap ("Row A binds no evaluable bytes/alignment pair, so postAlloc's arguments are"
+        ++ " not reconstructible")
+    | some args =>
+      let result := (contractAlloc canonicalEnvironment canonicalHeap).meaning args
+      if !codeIntactB canonicalEnvironment.image after then
+        .violated "postAlloc.CodeIntact(after)"
+      else
+        match result with
+        | .ok address =>
+          match postAllocMachineFailure? canonicalEnvironment args address before after with
+          | some clause => .violated clause
+          | none =>
+            .gap ("postAlloc.CodeIntact(after), x10=address, both cursor readings, the two"
+              ++ " containment bounds and WritesOnlyWithin(ownedRegion) all hold; but"
+              ++ " postAlloc.address≠0 / alignment≠0 / address%alignment=0 are functions of"
+              ++ " contractAlloc.meaning's own output at the reconstructed arguments and of no"
+              ++ " captured state (postAllocSuccessB_splits), so they cannot fail and this is NOT"
+              ++ " a pass")
+        | .error error =>
+          if after.regs.get? x10 != some (BitVec.ofNat 64 0) then .violated "postAlloc.x10=0"
+          else if !noAllocationB before after then .violated "postAlloc.NoAllocation"
+          else if !scalarWritesOnlyWithinB before after then
+            .violated "postAlloc.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"
+          else
+            .gap ("postAlloc.CodeIntact(after), x10=0, NoAllocation and WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"
+              ++ " all hold; postAlloc.error=outOfMemory is a tautology at a result taken from"
+              ++ " contractAlloc's own meaning (alloc_meaning_error_is_always_outOfMemory), and the"
+              ++ " outOfMemory arm was selected by a reconstructed argument rather than by the run,"
+              ++ " so this is NOT a pass")
+  | .allocatorFree =>
+    match postAllocatorFreeFailure? canonicalEnvironment
+        ((contractAllocatorFree canonicalEnvironment).meaning ()) before after with
+    | some clause => .violated clause
+    | none => .gap ("postAllocatorFree.CodeIntact(after)/NoAllocation/WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"
+        ++ " hold; postAllocatorFree.result=ok () is a tautology at a result taken from the"
+        ++ " contract's own meaning, so this is NOT a pass")
+  | .allocatorRemap =>
+    match postAllocatorRemapFailure? canonicalEnvironment
+        ((contractAllocatorRemap canonicalEnvironment).meaning ()) before after with
+    | some clause => .violated clause
+    | none => .gap ("postAllocatorRemap.CodeIntact(after)/NoAllocation/x10=0 hold;"
+        ++ " postAllocatorRemap.result=ok 0 is a tautology at a result taken from the contract's"
+        ++ " own meaning, so this is NOT a pass")
+  | .allocatorResize =>
+    match postAllocatorResizeFailure? canonicalEnvironment
+        ((contractAllocatorResize canonicalEnvironment).meaning ()) before after with
+    | some clause => .violated clause
+    | none => .gap ("postAllocatorResize.CodeIntact(after)/NoAllocation/x10=0 hold;"
+        ++ " postAllocatorResize.result=ok false is a tautology at a result taken from the"
+        ++ " contract's own meaning, so this is NOT a pass")
+
+/-- Column 4 for a results-family instance, with the same gate. `postRawError.code` compares the
+value the contract's own `meaning` produced against the observation that `meaning` was applied to, so
+it is `rfl`; `postRawResult.pointer` likewise. Neither can fail, so a clean run of both accessors'
+mirrors is a gap naming them, never a pass. The five frame conjuncts and `x10 = code` /
+`x10 = pointer` are real and any refutation from them stands. -/
+def resultsPostVerdict (results : ResultsFamily) (before after : State) : Verdict :=
+  match accessorFrameFailure? canonicalEnvironment (resultsRoutineName results) before after with
+  | some clause => .violated clause
+  | none =>
+    match globalsObservation? Elfling.canonicalDecoderGlobalsLayout before with
+    | none => .gap ("the five frame conjuncts hold; the decoder globals at the entry state do not"
+        ++ " encode any DecoderGlobalsModel, leaving the two result-arm conjuncts unevaluated")
+    | some observation =>
+      match results with
+      | .rawError =>
+        match postRawErrorFailure? canonicalEnvironment observation.statusCode
+            (.ok observation.statusCode) before after with
+        | some clause => .violated clause
+        | none => .gap ("the five frame conjuncts and postRawError.x10=code hold;"
+            ++ " postRawError.code=globals.last_status compares meaning's own output against the"
+            ++ " observation meaning was applied to, so it is rfl and cannot fail — NOT a pass")
+      | .rawResult =>
+        match postRawResultFailure? canonicalEnvironment Elfling.canonicalResultBuffer
+            observation.storedPresent
+            (.ok (if observation.storedPresent then Elfling.canonicalResultBuffer else 0))
+            before after with
+        | some clause => .violated clause
+        | none => .gap ("the five frame conjuncts and postRawResult.x10=pointer hold;"
+            ++ " postRawResult.pointer=stored?resultBuffer:0 compares meaning's own output against"
+            ++ " the observation meaning was applied to, so it is rfl and cannot fail — NOT a pass")
+
+/-- Column 4 for a validation-family instance, with the result clause gated.
+
+`canonicalOffsetsPost`'s `.ok` arm rests on `x10 = 0` settling the result clause *at every offset
+table*, which is genuine, but the rejecting arm's `error = invalidSsz` is satisfied by every result
+this meaning can produce (`meaningRequireCanonicalOffsets_onlyInvalid`) and so cannot fail. The pass
+is therefore downgraded; the refutations `canonicalOffsetsPost` produces are untouched. -/
+def canonicalOffsetsPostGated (index : Nat) (before after : State) : Verdict :=
+  match canonicalOffsetsPost index before after with
+  | .ok => .gap ("every LeafFrame conjunct holds and x10=0 settles the accepting arm at every"
+      ++ " offsets; but postCanonicalOffsets.error=invalidSsz is satisfied by every result this"
+      ++ " meaning can produce (meaningRequireCanonicalOffsets_onlyInvalid), so it cannot fail and"
+      ++ " this is NOT a pass")
+  | v => v
+
+/-! ## Per-instance rows: the unified dispatch
+
+Six families are decided here. Their tags are pairwise disjoint, so the arms below can be tried in
+sequence without either shadowing the other, and an unrecognised tag is still an explicit gap. -/
+
+def groundTruthRow (index : Nat) (o : FunctionInstance) : GroundTruthRow :=
+  let tag := tagOf index
+  let capture := captures[index]!
+  let family? := readFamily? tag
+  let alloc? := allocFamily? tag
+  let copy? := copyFamily? tag
+  let results? := resultsFamily? tag
+  let validation? := validationFamily? tag
+  -- The four emitted decoders carry all three of their columns together, because one argument
+  -- reconstruction feeds `pre`, `post` and `stepBound`.
+  let decoder? := (decoderFamily? tag).map fun family => decoderColumns family index capture
+  let entered : Verdict :=
+    match capture.entryState with
+    | some _ => .ok
+    | none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+  let exited : Verdict :=
+    if o.exitPcs.contains o.entryPc then .violated "entryPc is itself a declared exit"
+    else match capture.entryState, capture.exitPc with
+      | none, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+      | some _, none => .gap "entered but no declared exit reached before the sentinel"
+      | some _, some _ => .ok
+  let args? := capture.entryState.bind (readAtArgs? index)
+  let copyArgs?? := capture.entryState.bind (copyArgs? index)
+  let rowAOffset : Option Nat := do
+    let s ← capture.entryState
+    let row ← offsetBindingRow? index
+    bindingValue? row s
+  let outsideEveryFamily : Verdict :=
+    .gap ("tag " ++ tag ++ " is outside every checked family (read, allocator, copy, results,"
+      ++ " decoder, validation)")
+  let pre : Verdict :=
+    match decoder? with
+    | some (decoderPre, _, _) => decoderPre
+    | none =>
+      match copy?, capture.entryState with
+      | some copyFamily, some s => copyPreVerdict copyFamily index s
+      | some _, none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+      | none, _ =>
+        match alloc?, capture.entryState with
+        | some allocFamily, some s => allocPreVerdictGated index allocFamily s
+        | some _, none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+        | none, _ =>
+          match results?, capture.entryState with
+          | some _, none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+          | some .rawError, some s =>
+            (match preRawErrorFailure? canonicalEnvironment
+                Elfling.canonicalDecoderGlobalsLayout s with
+             | some clause => .violated clause
+             | none => .ok)
+          | some .rawResult, some s =>
+            (match preRawResultFailure? canonicalEnvironment
+                Elfling.canonicalDecoderGlobalsLayout s with
+             | some clause => .violated clause
+             | none => .ok)
+          | none, _ =>
+            match validation?, capture.entryState with
+            | some _, some s => canonicalOffsetsPre index s
+            | some _, none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+            | none, _ =>
+              match family?, capture.entryState with
+              | none, _ => outsideEveryFamily
+              | some _, none => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+              | some _, some s =>
+                match offsetBindingRow? index with
+                | none => .gap "Row A declares no offset binding for this instance"
+                | some row =>
+                  match bindingValue? row s with
+                  | none =>
+                    .gap ("Row A offset binding kind " ++ row.2.2.1 ++ " is not evaluable here")
+                  | some offset =>
+                    -- The `x12` conjunct is decided FIRST and on its own. `offset` is fixed by
+                    -- Row A, so this clause is refuted independently of `base`/`bytes`.
+                    if s.regs.get? x12 != some (BitVec.ofNat 64 offset) then
+                      .violated "preReadAt.x12=offset"
+                    else if bindingIsTautologicalAt index "offset" 12 then
+                      -- Not reachable on this artifact (Row A never binds a reader's `offset` to
+                      -- `x12`), but the gate is stated rather than assumed away.
+                      .gap ("x12 agrees with Row A, but Row A binds offset to x12 itself, so the"
+                        ++ " clause is x == x and cannot fail")
+                    else
+                      match args? with
+                      | none => .gap ("x12 agrees with Row A; the other conjuncts need the borrowed"
+                          ++ " slice, and x11 is not a materialisable length here")
+                      | some args =>
+                        match preReadAtFailure? canonicalEnvironment args s with
+                        | some clause => .violated clause
+                        | none => .ok
+  let realSteps : Option Nat := do
+    let entryStep ← capture.entryStep
+    let exitStep ← capture.exitStep
+    pure (exitStep - entryStep)
+  let stepBound : Option Nat :=
+    match decoder? with
+    | some (_, _, decoderBound) => decoderBound
+    | none =>
+      match family? with
+      | some family => some (readFamilyStepBound family o)
+      | none =>
+        match copy?, copyArgs?? with
+        | some copyFamily, some cargs => some (copyStepBound copyFamily cargs)
+        | some _, none => none
+        | none, _ =>
+          match alloc? with
+          | some allocFamily => some (allocFamilyStepBound allocFamily)
+          | none =>
+            match results? with
+            | some results => some (resultsFamilyStepBound results)
+            | none => none
+  let post : Verdict :=
+    match decoder? with
+    | some (_, decoderPost, _) => decoderPost
+    | none =>
+      match copy?, capture.entryState, capture.exitState, copyArgs?? with
+      | some _, none, _, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+      | some _, _, none, _ => .gap "no declared exit state captured"
+      | some _, _, _, none => .gap ("Row A dst/src/n bindings are not all evaluable here, or the"
+          ++ " source slice is unmaterialisable; no postCopy conjunct evaluated")
+      | some copyFamily, some before, some after, some cargs =>
+        -- `postCopyCheckedB_iff_postCopy` is an equivalence, so a `none` here really does say the
+        -- real `postCopy` holds at these arguments. It is the only column-4 pass in the module.
+        (match postCopyFailure? canonicalEnvironment cargs (copyMeaning copyFamily cargs)
+                before after with
+         | some clause => .violated clause
+         | none => .ok)
+      | none, _, _, _ =>
+        match alloc?, capture.entryState, capture.exitState with
+        | some _, none, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+        | some _, _, none => .gap "no declared exit state captured"
+        | some allocFamily, some before, some after =>
+          allocPostVerdictGated index allocFamily before after
+        | none, _, _ =>
+          match results?, capture.entryState, capture.exitState with
+          | some _, none, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+          | some _, _, none => .gap "no declared exit state captured"
+          | some results, some before, some after => resultsPostVerdict results before after
+          | none, _, _ =>
+            match validation?, capture.entryState, capture.exitState with
+            | some _, none, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+            | some _, _, none => .gap "no declared exit state captured"
+            | some _, some before, some after => canonicalOffsetsPostGated index before after
+            | none, _, _ =>
+              match family?, capture.entryState, capture.exitState, args? with
+              | none, _, _, _ => outsideEveryFamily
+              | some _, none, _, _ => .gap "never entered on this arm"
+              | some _, _, none, _ => .gap "no declared exit state captured"
+              | some _, _, _, none => .gap "arguments not reconstructible"
+              | some family, some before, some after, some args =>
+                match scalarWidth? family, scalarMeaning family args with
+                | some width, some result =>
+                  (match postScalarReadFailure? canonicalEnvironment args width result
+                          before after with
+                   | some clause => .violated clause
+                   | none =>
+                     -- A passing `.error` arm is NOT a pass, and a passing `.ok` arm is not one
+                     -- either: `postScalarReadCheckedB` is proved only in the refuting direction,
+                     -- so `mirror = true` does not give `postScalarRead`.
+                     match result with
+                     | .error _ => .gap ("meaning errors at the witness args; postScalarRead's"
+                         ++ " error arm is then trivially satisfied and says nothing about the run")
+                     | .ok _ => .ok)
+                | _, _ =>
+                  match family with
+                  | .bytesAt =>
+                    (match capture.entryState.bind (bytesAtArgs? index) with
+                     | none =>
+                       match leafFrameSharedFailure? canonicalEnvironment args.base args.bytes
+                           before after with
+                       | some clause => .violated clause
+                       | none => .gap ("LeafFrame.MemoryBytes/CodeIntact/NoAllocation hold; Row A"
+                           ++ " binds no evaluable len, leaving"
+                           ++ " LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord and"
+                           ++ " postBytesAt.x10=base+offset / postBytesAt.x11=length unevaluated")
+                     | some bytesArgs =>
+                       let result := (contractBytesAt canonicalEnvironment).meaning bytesArgs
+                       match postBytesAtFailure? canonicalEnvironment bytesArgs result
+                           before after with
+                       | some clause => .violated clause
+                       | none =>
+                         match result with
+                         | .error _ => .gap ("meaning errors at the witness args; postBytesAt's"
+                             ++ " error arm is then trivially satisfied and says nothing about the"
+                             ++ " run")
+                         | .ok _ => .ok)
+                  | _ =>
+                    match leafFrameSharedFailure? canonicalEnvironment args.base args.bytes
+                        before after with
+                    | some clause => .violated clause
+                    | none => .gap ("LeafFrame.MemoryBytes/CodeIntact/NoAllocation hold for " ++ tag
+                        ++ "; LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord(resultBase,width) and the"
+                        ++ " result-slot clause need a resultBase Row A does not pin")
+  let steps : Verdict :=
+    match realSteps, stepBound with
+    | some real, some bound => if real ≤ bound then .ok else .violated "used > stepBound args"
+    | none, _ => .gap "no entry/exit pair captured"
+    | _, none =>
+      if validation?.isSome then canonicalOffsetsSteps realSteps
+      else if copy?.isSome then
+        .gap "copy stepBound needs the length argument, which is not reconstructible here"
+      else .gap "no stepBound (tag outside every checked family)"
+  { index := index, routineTag := tag, entryPc := o.entryPc
+    entered := entered, pre := pre, exited := exited, post := post, steps := steps
+    realSteps := realSteps, stepBound := stepBound, exitPc := capture.exitPc
+    entryX10 := capture.entryState.bind (fun s => (registerValue? s 10).map BitVec.toNat)
+    entryX11 := capture.entryState.bind (fun s => (registerValue? s 11).map BitVec.toNat)
+    entryX12 := capture.entryState.bind (fun s => (registerValue? s 12).map BitVec.toNat)
+    rowAOffset := rowAOffset }
+
+def groundTruthRows : Array GroundTruthRow :=
+  generatedProgram.functionInstances.zipIdx.map fun (o, i) => groundTruthRow i o
+
+
+/-! ## Rendering -/
+
+private def pad (n : Nat) (s : String) : String :=
+  if s.length ≥ n then s else s ++ String.ofList (List.replicate (n - s.length) ' ')
+
+/-- A `pre` pass is rendered distinctly wherever some conjunct is true at arguments the harness
+itself supplied. That is the read family (`base`/`bytes` witness-constructed on three of five
+conjuncts) and the copy family (`contents` witness-constructed on two of six). The two exported
+accessors carry no such caveat — their `pre` mirrors are quantified over every ghost model, so
+nothing about them is witness-constructed — and neither do the three constant allocator thunks,
+whose `pre` is `CodeIntact` alone. Those render as a plain `ok`.
+
+A conjunct that is `x == x` is **not** covered by this marker. Those rows are gaps, decided in
+`copyPreVerdict` / `allocPreVerdictGated`, and never reach here as `.ok`. -/
+private def renderPre (tag : String) : Verdict → String
+  | .ok =>
+      if (readFamily? tag).isSome || (copyFamily? tag).isSome then "ok@witness-args" else "ok"
+  | v => v.render
+
+/-- A `post` `ok` is reported only where the mirror is proved as an **equivalence**, so it really
+does say the predicate holds at the arguments shown. -/
+private def renderPost : Verdict → String
+  | v => v.render
+
+def GroundTruthRow.render (r : GroundTruthRow) : String :=
+  String.intercalate " | "
+    [ pad 3 (toString r.index)
+    , pad 22 r.routineTag
+    , pad 6 (toString r.entryPc)
+    , pad 34 r.entered.render
+    , pad 46 (renderPre r.routineTag r.pre)
+    , pad 44 r.exited.render
+    , pad 50 (renderPost r.post)
+    , pad 30 r.steps.render
+    , pad 6 (r.realSteps.elim "-" toString)
+    , pad 6 (r.stepBound.elim "-" toString)
+    , pad 21 (r.entryX10.elim "-" toString)
+    , pad 21 (r.entryX11.elim "-" toString)
+    , pad 21 (r.entryX12.elim "-" toString)
+    , pad 12 (r.rowAOffset.elim "-" toString) ]
+
+def header : String :=
+  String.intercalate " | "
+    [ pad 3 "idx", pad 22 "routineTag", pad 6 "entry", pad 34 "1 entered"
+    , pad 46 "2 pre", pad 44 "3 exited", pad 50 "4 post", pad 30 "5 steps"
+    , pad 6 "real", pad 6 "bound"
+    , pad 21 "x10@entry", pad 21 "x11@entry", pad 21 "x12@entry", pad 12 "RowA offset" ]
+
+private def tally (f : GroundTruthRow → Verdict) : String :=
+  toString (groundTruthRows.filter fun r => (f r).isOk).size ++ " / " ++
+    toString (groundTruthRows.filter fun r => (f r).isViolated).size ++ " / " ++
+    toString (groundTruthRows.filter fun r =>
+      !(f r).isOk && !(f r).isViolated).size
+
+def report : String :=
+  String.intercalate "\n"
+    ([ "## 2. Contract ground truth — real states from the Sail model"
+     , ""
+     , "Run: corpus case `" ++ captureCaseId ++ "`, " ++ toString captureInput.size
+         ++ " input bytes, outcome " ++ (match captureOutcome with
+            | .reached n => "reached the sentinel after " ++ toString n ++ " retired steps"
+            | .trapped => "TRAPPED"
+            | .exhausted => "fuel EXHAUSTED")
+     , ""
+     , "Legend."
+     , ""
+     , "`ok@witness-args` — the precondition evaluated true, but at arguments the harness itself"
+     , "supplied on some conjunct: `base`/`bytes` in the read family (three of five conjuncts),"
+     , "`contents` in the copy family (two of six). Only a FAIL is conclusive there."
+     , ""
+     , "`ok` in column 4 — the mirror is proved as an EQUIVALENCE with the real postcondition"
+     , "(`postScalarReadCheckedB_iff_postScalarRead`, `postBytesAtCheckedB_iff_postBytesAt`,"
+     , "`postCopyCheckedB_iff_postCopy`), so it really does say `post` holds at those arguments."
+     , "Where only a `Prop -> Bool` mirror exists, a clean run renders as a gap, not a pass."
+     , ""
+     , "A conjunct that CANNOT FAIL never renders as a pass. Row A binding a parameter to the very"
+     , "register the contract names makes that conjunct `x == x`"
+     , "(`register_conjunct_is_a_tautology_at_a_reg_binding`); a clause computed from the contract's"
+     , "own `meaning` at the same arguments is `rfl`; `postAlloc`'s `address≠0`/`alignment≠0`/"
+     , "`address%alignment=0` mention no captured state at all (`postAllocSuccessB_splits`). Every"
+     , "such row is a `gap` whose text names the offending conjuncts. Refutations are unaffected:"
+     , "an unfalsifiable conjunct never fails, so any clause a mirror names is a real one."
+     , ""
+     , "A post FAIL naming a `LeafFrame.*` clause holds at every result record, so it does not"
+     , "depend on a `resultBase` the artifact leaves unpinned. A `gap` is never a pass, and each"
+     , "gap names the specific conjuncts left unevaluated."
+     , ""
+     , "`post` is reported independently of `pre`: at a row whose `pre` is refuted the obligation"
+     , "says nothing, so read those `post` cells as evidence about the run and not about the claim."
+     , ""
+     , "```"
+     , header
+     , String.ofList (List.replicate 340 '-') ] ++
+     (groundTruthRows.map GroundTruthRow.render).toList ++
+     [ "```"
+     , ""
+     , "totals (ok / violated / gap):"
+     , "```"
+     , "  1 entered : " ++ tally (·.entered)
+     , "  2 pre     : " ++ tally (·.pre)
+     , "  3 exited  : " ++ tally (·.exited)
+     , "  4 post    : " ++ tally (·.post)
+     , "  5 steps   : " ++ tally (·.steps)
+     , "```"
+     , "" ])
