+The two passes are `memcpy` (139) and `memmove` (140). They are reported as passes only because
+`postCopyCheckedB_iff_postCopy` is an **equivalence**, so a clean mirror really does give the real
+`postCopy`; `copy_post_result_clause_is_not_vacuous` separately shows the destination did not
+already hold the copied bytes, and `copy_post_check_flips_on_every_conjunct` exhibits every conjunct
+firing. `rawAlloc` (0) would have been a third pass and is gated: three of `postAlloc`'s success-arm
+conjuncts mention no captured state at all (`postAllocSuccessB_splits`). -/
+theorem post_refutations_and_the_two_passes :
+    ((groundTruthRows.filterMap fun r =>
+      if r.post.isViolated then some (r.index, r.routineTag, r.entryPc, r.post) else none),
+     (groundTruthRows.filterMap fun r =>
+      if r.post.isOk then some (r.index, r.routineTag, r.entryPc) else none)) =
+      (#[(48, "bytesAt", 72232, .violated "LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"),
+         (49, "readU64", 72232, .violated "LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"),
+         (50, "bytesAt", 72332, .violated "LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"),
+         (59, "bytesAt", 73620, .violated "postBytesAt.x11=length"),
+         (66, "readOffset", 73904, .violated "postScalarRead.x10=value"),
+         (67, "readU32", 73904, .violated "postScalarRead.x10=value"),
+         (68, "readOffset", 73952, .violated "postScalarRead.x10=value"),
+         (69, "readU32", 73952, .violated "postScalarRead.x10=value"),
+         (77, "bytesAt", 74472, .violated "LeafFrame.WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord"),
+         (89, "bytesAt", 75336, .violated "postBytesAt.x11=length"),
+         (136, "allocatorAlloc", 79720, .violated "postAlloc.x10=0")],
+       #[(139, "memcpy", 81592), (140, "memmove", 81628)]) := by native_decide
+
+/-- **The three gated rows, as gaps.** `rawAlloc`'s `pre` and `post` and the two copy rows' `pre`
+each evaluated with no failing conjunct and are still not passes. Pinned as `isOk = false` so the
+gate cannot silently stop working: if a future edit lets any of them reach `.ok`, this theorem
+fails. -/
+theorem the_gated_rows_are_gaps_not_passes :
+    ([0, 139, 140].map fun index =>
+      (index, groundTruthRows[index]!.pre.isOk, groundTruthRows[index]!.pre.isViolated,
+       groundTruthRows[index]!.post.isOk, groundTruthRows[index]!.post.isViolated)) =
