+/-- **All five clauses of the cursor block fire, and the real readings pass.** Swapping the two cursor
+values breaks monotonicity; a zero-byte, one-alignment request makes the observed 32-byte advance
+exceed its own bound; putting the address below the starting cursor breaks containment from the left;
+a 48-byte request breaks it from the right; a byte changed at address `0` breaks the exact write
+frame. -/
