+/-- **All four failure-arm clauses fire, and three of them are informative.** The real exit state
+fails `x10 = 0`; zeroing `x10` makes the whole arm report no failure, which witnesses that
+`NoAllocation` and the leaf frame already held; disturbing the cursor word then fires `NoAllocation`;
+changing a byte at address `0` fires the leaf frame. The fourth, `error = outOfMemory`, fires only at
+a hand-made `.error .invalidSsz` — with `result` taken from the contract's own `meaning` it is a
