+
+`memcpy` (139) and `memmove` (140) are the first rows in this harness whose `post` reaches `ok`. A
+pass is the outcome that most needs interrogating, so everything below is written to say exactly what
+that `ok` does and does not cover, and each conjunct is exhibited failing on a counterfactual. -/
+
+-- The evidence records below are wide tuples of tuples, and `DecidableEq` for them exceeds the
+-- default instance-search size. Purely a search budget: it changes which instances are *found*, not
+-- which exist, and every theorem below still discharges by `native_decide` on a concrete value.
+set_option synthInstance.maxSize 4000
+
+/-- The 14 `kind := "emitted"` instances: the only ones reached through a real call, and therefore the
+only ones at which a register-based precondition is a question rather than a category error. The
+other 127 are `kind := "inlined"`, where no call occurs and the compiler was free to keep a value
+anywhere. -/
+theorem emitted_instances_and_their_tags :
+    (generatedManifest.filterMap fun m =>
+      if m.kind == "emitted" then some (m.index, m.routineTag) else none) =
+      #[(0, "rawAlloc"), (1, "zesuDecodeRaw"), (5, "allocatorFree"), (6, "decodeRaw"),
+        (123, "allocatorRemap"), (124, "optionalU64"), (126, "byteListList"),
+        (134, "requireCanonicalOffsets"), (135, "allocatorResize"), (136, "allocatorAlloc"),
+        (137, "rawError"), (138, "rawResult"), (139, "memcpy"), (140, "memmove")] := by
+  native_decide
+
+/-- **This claim was true of the copy family alone and is false of the integrated harness.**
+
+The copy agent recorded `no_emitted_row_carries_a_pre_refutation = #[]`. At the time the only emitted
+rows any family decided were `memcpy` and `memmove`, and their register clauses held. Wiring the
+allocator and validation families adds two emitted rows that *do* refute, so the corrected statement
+is below — and it is a stronger finding than the original rather than a weaker one, because it puts
+two `pre` refutations at real call boundaries, where the ABI genuinely applies.
+
+What survives unchanged is the sharper claim: none of the **100 `preReadAt.x12=offset`** refutations
+is on an emitted row (`x12_refutations_are_all_on_inlined_instances`). The read family's register
+discipline still has no call boundary on this artifact at which it could be tested at all. -/
+theorem emitted_rows_carrying_a_pre_refutation :
+    (groundTruthRows.filterMap fun r =>
+      if r.pre.isViolated && (generatedManifest[r.index]!).kind == "emitted" then
+        some (r.index, r.routineTag, r.pre) else none) =
+      #[(134, "requireCanonicalOffsets", .violated "preCanonicalOffsets.MemoryBytes"),
+        (136, "allocatorAlloc", .violated "preAlloc.x10=bytes")] := by native_decide
+
+/-- **Where Row A puts each copy argument, beside the register `preCopy` names.**
+
+For all six (`dst`, `src`, `n` at each of the two instances) Row A's effective binding is exactly the
+register the contract constrains — `x10`/`x11`/`x12`. That is a real, independently obtained
+agreement: the identical comparison is what refutes 100 read-family rows, where Row A answers
+`x9`/`x18`/`x19`/`x24`/`x27` or a constant against the contract's `x12`.
+
+The consequence is stated rather than hidden: **because the register agrees, the numeric conjunct
+`x10 = destination` is true by construction** at these arguments, since `destination` *is* what
+`bindingValue?` read out of `x10`. The information is in the register numbers, not in the numeric
+comparison. -/
+theorem copy_bindings_name_the_registers_preCopy_constrains :
+    ([139, 140].flatMap fun index =>
+      ["dst", "src", "n"].map fun name =>
+        (index, name, (bindingRow? index name).map fun r => (r.2.2.1, r.2.2.2.1))) =
+      [(139, "dst", some ("reg", (10 : Int))), (139, "src", some ("reg", 11)),
+       (139, "n", some ("reg", 12)),
+       (140, "dst", some ("reg", 10)), (140, "src", some ("reg", 11)),
+       (140, "n", some ("reg", 12))] := by native_decide
+
+/-- **One of those six agreements is circular and must not be counted as evidence.**
+
+`memmove`'s `n` has NO DWARF location — the raw row is `callerProvided`. Its effective `reg 12` was
+manufactured by the extractor's `riscvCAbiArg2` recovery, i.e. by applying the very RISC-V C ABI rule
+that `preCopy`'s `x12 = length` conjunct states. Row A and the contract therefore agree there because
+they were told the same thing, not because two sources concur. It is the only `riscvCAbiArg2`
+recovery in the whole artifact, and the other five bindings are raw DWARF. -/
+theorem memmove_length_binding_is_abi_recovered_not_dwarf :
+    ((Elfling.GeneratedBindings.rawBindings.filter fun r => r.1 == 139 || r.1 == 140),
+     (Elfling.GeneratedBindings.recoveredBindings.filter fun r =>
+        r.2.2.1 == "riscvCAbiArg2")) =
+      ([(139, "dst", "reg", 10, 0), (139, "src", "reg", 11, 0), (139, "n", "reg", 12, 0),
+        (140, "dst", "reg", 10, 0), (140, "src", "reg", 11, 0),
+        (140, "n", "callerProvided", -1, 0)],
+       [(140, "n", "riscvCAbiArg2", "reg", 12, 0)]) := by native_decide
