+*The ownership clause, and this is a limitation of row 139 rather than of the check.* `memcpy`'s
+destination `0x3000_000f_f398 + 256` lies wholly **inside the canonical stack**, which the clause
+permits anyway, so shrinking its record to `0` still passes (`true`, no violating address —
+`2 ^ 64`). At row 139 `WritesOnlyWithinOwnRecord(destination, length)` is therefore no stronger than
