+the harness's runner past the sentinel with two direct calls is exactly the missing ingredient, and
+nothing about the contracts or the reconstruction has to change for it. -/
+theorem results_family_are_call_graph_roots :
+    (resultsFamilyCallGraph, resultsFamilyCallers) =
+      (#[(137, none, #[], #[], #[]), (138, none, #[], #[], #[])], #[]) := by native_decide
+
+/-- The two accessors' manifest facts: index, tag, `kind`, entry pc, and whether the capture entered
+them. -/
+def resultsFamilyRows : Array (Nat × String × String × Nat × Bool) :=
+  #[137, 138].map fun index =>
+    (index, (generatedManifest[index]!).routineTag, (generatedManifest[index]!).kind,
+      (generatedManifest[index]!).entryPc, (captures[index]!).entryState.isSome)
+
+/-- **Both results-family instances are emitted, and neither is entered.** `kind = "emitted"` is what
+distinguishes these from the 127 inlined rows on which a register-based precondition is a category
+error; `entered = false` is why the wiring below cannot be exercised by this run. -/
+theorem results_family_rows_are_emitted_and_never_entered :
+    resultsFamilyRows =
+      #[(137, "rawError", "emitted", 79744, false),
+        (138, "rawResult", "emitted", 79756, false)] := by native_decide
+
+/-- The three verdict columns the results-family wiring touches, plus the step bound, for indices 137
+and 138 in that order. (Their index, tag, `kind` and entry pc are pinned separately, just above.) -/
+def resultsFamilyVerdicts : Array (String × String × String × Option Nat) :=
+  #[137, 138].map fun index =>
+    let r := groundTruthRows[index]!
+    (r.pre.render, r.post.render, r.steps.render, r.stepBound)
+
+/-- **What the wiring changed for indices 137 and 138: the gap *reason*, and nothing else.** Both
+rows were `gap(tag … is outside the checked read family)` in columns 2 and 4 and carried no
+`stepBound`; they are now capture-gaps carrying the contracts' own step bounds (16 and 32). No column
+total moves, because a gap was and remains a gap — which is exactly the point. -/
+theorem results_family_verdicts :
+    resultsFamilyVerdicts =
+      #[("gap(never entered on this arm)", "gap(never entered on this arm)",
+         "gap(no entry/exit pair captured)", some 16),
+        ("gap(never entered on this arm)", "gap(never entered on this arm)",
+         "gap(no entry/exit pair captured)", some 32)] := by native_decide
