+indices 6 and 126. They do not, and `alloc_binding_reading_is_an_address_not_a_value` shows exactly
+how that reading arises: `bindingValue?` on the `alloc` row returns `69292065`, the word *stored at*
+the location, while the location itself — which is what `EntryArgs.allocatorBase` and
+`CollectionArgs.allocatorBase` mean — is `52776559179248`, precisely `x11`. Feeding the former into
+`preEntry.x11=allocatorBase` manufactures a refutation out of a DWARF reading error. -/
